cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its reported results, please cite this repository and record the commit used."
type: software
title: "Outcome-aware context allocation: a local experiment in pre-answer evidence budgets"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-15"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/outcome-aware-context-allocation"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/outcome-aware-context-allocation"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Research software for selecting two or ten retrieved paragraphs before a
  local language model answers. A small controller learns the difference in
  strict answer-and-support success between paired evidence budgets. On 480
  protected HotpotQA distractor questions, the outcome-trained controller had
  14 strict successes and a controller trained on cheaper support-coverage labels
  had 17. Sparse
  strict outcomes and invalid wall-time measurements leave the efficiency
  comparison inconclusive. The original full-family assignment is incomplete
  and unscored. A separately frozen 64-question reader validation found 19
  strict successes with an authored evidence-first prompt versus 6 with the
  unchanged reader prompt, at 2.72 versus 2.59 seconds per query. Its strict
  endpoint interval was positive, but the full reader admission gate failed
  the answer-preservation guard. No new allocation advantage is established.
  The repository provides the evaluation harness, frozen
  configuration, aggregate findings and qualified provenance; full raw-result
  authentication requires retained research assets outside the public release.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - context allocation
  - outcome-aware routing
  - evidence budgets
  - reproducible research
  - inconclusive results
